    "body": "### Hi Steemers! You never knew the real value of honey, so listen up.\n## Honey\n---\nHoney is a natural product obtained as a result of processing by bees of flower nectar, secreted by the honey glands of plants in the flowering period. The main components of honey are fructose and glucose. They give the honey a unique sweet taste.\nhttp://vkusneedoma.ru/wp-content/uploads/2012/07/%D0%9A%D0%BE%D0%BC%D1%83-%D0%BC%D0%B5%D0%B4-%D0%B2%D1%80%D0%B5%D0%B4%D0%B5%D0%BD1.jpg\n<a href=\"http://vkusneedoma.ru/wp-content/uploads/2012/07/%D0%9A%D0%BE%D0%BC%D1%83-%D0%BC%D0%B5%D0%B4-%D0%B2%D1%80%D0%B5%D0%B4%D0%B5%D0%BD1.jpg\">Image url</a> \n\nBiochemists have proven that the human body metabolizes these substances is much better than sucrose. Honey is lighter than sugar, is passed by the kidneys, does not irritate the mucous membrane of the stomach and intestines and, finally, rapidly releases energy. Glucose and fructose dilate blood vessels, contribute to the regulation of nervous activity, improve nutrition of the heart muscle. \n\nAlso, the honey contains pollen and enzymes produced by bees. This wonderful natural combination of honey determines its unique properties: it strengthens the immune system, gives strength, improves appetite, heals wounds, soothes, and the constant use of honey instead of sugar contributes to weight loss.\n### <em> <blockquote>If you want to stay young, be sure to eat honey. (Avicenna)</blockquote></em>\n\nBeneficial properties has only natural honey, that is a natural product, has not passed any technological processing. Heating honey above 36\u00b0C (temperature of the hive) destroys its beneficial properties.\n\nOur ancestors called honey a gift from the gods. Mention of its healing properties can be found in the records of Egyptian physicians, in the Bible, in the texts of Hippocrates and the Koran. The Greeks believed that Zeus was fed honey from the same place the expression goes, \"Honey \u2013 food of the gods\".  <em><b>About this I was told since childhood. </b> </em>\n\n<em>I like bees and honey. \n\n<em>Thank you for your attention!\n\n<em>@kental with you!\n\n<em>Let's learn beekeeping together!\n\n<em><a href=\"https://steemit.com/@kental\">Follow me</a> If you want to learn more about beekeeping! </em>\n\nMy Previous Article about <a href=\"https://steemit.com/honey/@kental/three-of-the-most-healing-honey-kinds-honey-in-medicine-the-kinds-of-honey\">Three of the Most Healing Honey Kinds. Honey in Medicine.</a>",
